§ CSLv3_CSSLv3_BRIDGE
I> CSLv3 = dense spec / reasoning notation (THIS repo)
I> CSSLv3 = programming language at C:\Users\Apocky\source\repos\CSSLv3
I> this spec describes the interop contract between the two
I> read-only reference : CSSLv3\specs\SYNTHESIS_V2.csl + CSSLv3\specs\09_SYNTAX.csl
W! this file lives in CSLv3 -- we do NOT write to the CSSLv3 repo
W! both sides round-trip via cslparser (this repo's reference implementation)

§ LAYERING
  # user-facing code       : CSSLv3 (.cssl / .cssl-rust / .cssl-csl)
  # chain-of-thought       : CSLv3 inside CoT-comments
  # spec documents         : CSLv3 (.csl) at project level
  I> CSSLv3 carries the running program ; CSLv3 carries the reasoning

§ INTEGRATION-SURFACES

§§ S1-CoT-IN-CSSLv3-SOURCE
  # Per CSSLv3 09_SYNTAX CoT-IN-COMMENTS section, a CSSLv3 source file may
  # embed CSLv3 inside comment forms:
  #   (a) block-CoT       §-brace...§-brace   (multi-line)
  #   (b) line-CoT        § I> | § W! | § N!  until EOL
  # Compiler-default: treat as comment, emit nothing into HIR.
  # With --lint-csl, the comment bodies are handed to cslparser for
  # parse-validation; any error is surfaced at editor-level.
  # IDE tooling highlights the § + W! + N! + I> as structural tokens.
  W! authors use CSLv3 ¬ English for rationale in CSSLv3 source
  # (density = sovereignty ; CC8 in SYNTHESIS_V2)

§§ S2-FORMATTER-ROUND-TRIP
  # Per CSSLv3 09_SYNTAX COMPILER-GLYPH-OPS section, the CSSLv3 formatter
  # (csslfmt) round-trips ASCII-form and Unicode-form of shared glyphs.
  # Mapping (informational ; canonical list in specs/12_TOKENIZER.csl):
  #
  #   ASCII       Unicode     semantic
  #   ->          arrow       fn-arrow / flow
  #   =>          dbl-arrow   implies / match-arm
  #   ::          dbl-colon   path-sep / has-type
  #   !=          neq         not-equal
  #   <=          le          lte
  #   >=          ge          gte
  #   all         forall      universal quantifier
  #   any         exists      existential quantifier
  #   |>          triangle    pipeline
  #   &&          and         logical-and
  #   ||          or          logical-or
  #   ~           not         negation
  #   in          in          set-membership
  #
  # Storage form : Unicode UTF-8 (canonical).
  # Formatter R! : auto-upgrade ASCII to Unicode on save.
  # Round-trip invariant: parse → format → parse ≡ same-HIR.
  # Reuse        : the alias table in 12_TOKENIZER.csl is the shared source
  #                of truth (74 entries after Session 3 expansion).

§§ S3-PARSER-REUSE
  # cslparser binary  : parser.exe produced by `odin build parser/`
  # cslparser library : Odin package `cslparser` (parser/*.odin)
  # CLI surface :
  #   --errors      silent if clean ; file:line:col diagnostics otherwise
  #   --tokens      lexer-only dump
  #   --semantic    semantic pass : morphemes, aliases, scope, validity
  #   --roundtrip   parse → print → reparse → AST-shape-equal
  #   --print       reprint through pretty-printer
  #   --mode=X      X in {canonical, compact, literate, ascii-only, unicode-only}
  # CSSLv3 consumes cslparser to:
  #   (a) validate block-CoT and line-CoT bodies under --lint-csl
  #   (b) normalise CoT glyphs (ASCII vs Unicode) during csslfmt
  #   (c) surface CoT blocks to Claude-instance tooling as AST,
  #       not as opaque text.

§§ LINT-PROTOCOL-Session-4-T19
  # cssllint subcommand : `parser cssllint [--json] [--strict] [--strict-parse] <file>`
  # Produces machine-readable diagnostics suitable for CSSLv3 compiler
  # embedding. --json emits a single JSON object conforming to the schema:
  #
  #   {
  #     "file":   <string>,
  #     "status": "ok" | "warn" | "error",
  #     "counts": { "info": N, "warn": N, "error": N },
  #     "diags":  [
  #       { "line": <int>, "col": <int>, "sev": "info"|"warn"|"error",
  #         "code": <string>, "msg": <string> }
  #     ]
  #   }
  #
  # Diagnostic-code namespace :
  #   CSL-E-LEX       lexer error
  #   CSL-E-PARSE     parse error
  #   CSL-E-002       morpheme-duplicate (always-error)
  #   CSL-E-IO        file-read error
  #   CSL-W-001       morpheme-order
  #   CSL-W-003       morpheme-unknown
  #   CSL-W-004       slot-arity
  #   CSL-W-005       evidence-contradict
  #   CSL-W-007       permissive-accept
  #   CSL-I-006       compound-assoc (info-only)
  #
  # Exit-code contract :
  #   0  status == "ok" or "warn" (sev flag lint/default)
  #   1  status == "error" OR (--strict AND any-warn) OR (--strict-parse-specific)
  #
  # CSSLv3 tooling usage pattern :
  #   $ parser cssllint --json src.cssl > diags.json
  #   (parse diags.json ; render inline in IDE ; gate CI on status != "ok")
  #
  # Schema stability : tied to CSLv3 minor version.
  # Adding new diag codes is backward-compatible; renaming is a major bump.

§ HANDOFF-DATA-MODEL
  # When CSSLv3 tooling hands a CoT block to cslparser :
  #   input  : raw source bytes of the block body (delimiters stripped)
  #   output : Node tree with kind in {Section, Directive, Relation, ...}
  #   errors : []Parse_Error ; non-empty implies the body is malformed CSLv3
  # Reverse direction : cslparser pretty-printer emits bytes ;
  # CSSLv3 can reinsert verbatim.

§ VERSIONING
  # CSSLv3 is a separate repository ; its 00-23 specs evolve independently.
  # CSLv3 ships here as a stable notation with its own semver.
  # Bridge contract = THIS file + specs/12_TOKENIZER.csl alias table.
  W! alias-table change -> bump CSLv3 minor ; CSSLv3 consumes-major-compatible
  R! CSSLv3 may later self-host its CoT formatter
  # (the contract stabilises the glyph table, not the implementation.)

§ NON-GOALS
  N! CSLv3 does NOT import or execute CSSLv3 code
  N! CSSLv3 source is NOT a CSLv3 document
  # (only CoT bodies and § I>/W!/N! lines are CSLv3-parseable.)
  N! CSLv3 specs do NOT describe CSSLv3 semantics
  # (those live in CSSLv3's own specs/ tree.)

§ INVARIANTS
  t_inf : CSLv3-glyph-inventory = one source of truth  -- specs/12_TOKENIZER.csl
  t_inf : CSLv3-grammar         = one source of truth  -- specs/02_GRAMMAR.csl + 13
  t_inf : cslparser             = reference implementation
  t_inf : density = sovereignty -- CC8 of CSSLv3 SYNTHESIS_V2

